# Only the two live data directories, not data/ as a whole. data/snapshots/ and
# data/dev_seed/ are tracked on purpose: the first pins the ML evaluation inputs
# so results stay comparable, the second is what lets a fresh clone serve at all.
# Both are immutable, and the deploy excludes data/ entirely, so neither can
# reach the server or be overwritten by the weekly cron.
data/raw/
data/processed/
logs/

# Generated artifacts, with three exceptions below.
#
# Most of outputs/ is experiment scratch: plots from hypotheses already settled
# and multi-megabyte CV dumps. Git keeps every version forever, so committing
# those grows the repo permanently for files nobody reads twice.
#
# The accuracy reports are a different thing wearing the same coat. They are the
# recorded score of each model version, the numbers the design doc's version log
# cites and the Forecast Validation page reads. Untracked, the evidence for
# "this model beats the spreadsheet" lived in one working directory and was one
# `rm -rf outputs/` from gone. Together they are 130 KB.
#
# ml_backtest_weekly.csv is the per-week detail underneath ml_accuracy_by_sku,
# and the script that writes it refuses unless the two reconcile exactly, so it
# is the same evidence at a finer grain rather than a separate artifact. It is
# also the file a fresh clone needs for the backtest chart to draw anything: the
# planning service treats it as optional and degrades to a totals-only view, so
# untracked it made a working feature look unbuilt on every machine but this one.
# At 430 KB it is larger than the pair above and rewritten per model version,
# which is a real cost accepted deliberately rather than overlooked.
#
# Written as outputs/* rather than outputs/, because git cannot re-include a
# file whose parent directory is excluded.
outputs/*
!outputs/reports/
outputs/reports/*
!outputs/reports/ml_accuracy.csv
!outputs/reports/ml_accuracy_by_sku.csv
!outputs/reports/ml_backtest_weekly.csv

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.env
.venv/
*.egg-info/
.DS_Store
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.claude/
